/**
 * components/shared/AnalyticsPage.js: creator growth and engagement dashboard.
 *
 * TikTok, YouTube and Instagram: follower trend with forecast, milestone ETAs, traffic sources,
 * top videos, campaign performance. Admins pick any creator; creators see only their own.
 *
 * @gotcha every platform is normalised to ONE shape before any chart sees it: `profileAll` rows
 *         of {date, followers_count, net_followers} and `videos` rows of {video_id, total_play}.
 *         Normalise a new platform into that shape; never teach a chart about a platform.
 * @gotcha this is the ONE frontend surface that reads platform-specific raw feeds. Everything
 *         else goes through video_stats. Do not copy a raw tiktok_ or yt_ read out of here.
 * @gotcha neither Instagram nor YouTube reports historical follower counts, so both anchor at
 *         today's total and cumulate deltas backward. Instagram's feed caps at 30 days, so a
 *         missed run is lost history rather than a gap to refill.
 * @see docs/CODEBASE.md Platform Independence
 */
